{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Bagger, Christoffer","Sekara, Vedran","Skadegård, Tess"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-515396"],"event":{"end":"2016-04-28","start":"2016-04-28","title":"Bodies. Big Data. Believers.","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"girl meets boy or elderly gentleman what big data can tell us about the gender age gap in romantic comedy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://koensforskning.soc.ku.dk/koordinationens-arrangementer/aarskonference2016/workshops/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-515396","ids":["ku-cc381fe2-98a5-4f3b-a047-815e7a019eed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9047DA145CB780213FFA9EB9EA1C242C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://koensforskning.soc.ku.dk/koordinationens-arrangementer/aarskonference2016/workshops/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Study board of Media, Cognition and Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer","key":"baggerpau","last":"Bagger","locid":"ab897ab2-3fc0-4b94-9a66-73abe6da1be5","name":"Bagger, Christoffer","orcid":"0000-0001-9733-168X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Vedran","key":"sekarapau","last":"Sekara","name":"Sekara, Vedran","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tess","key":"skadegårdpau","last":"Skadegård","name":"Skadegård, Tess","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cc381fe2-98a5-4f3b-a047-815e7a019eed"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Girl meets boy (or elderly gentleman) : What Big Data can tell us about the gender-age gap in Romantic Comedy","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-515396","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"NETWORKS are everywhere. From the smallest confines of the cells within our bodies to the webs of social relations across the globe. Networks are not static, they constantly change, adapt, and evolve to suit new conditions. In order to understand the fundamental laws that govern networks we need new, highly detailed maps that uncover the interactions of all constituents, accurately and in a temporal manner. One of the hardest networks to understand, but also one of the most interesting ones, is the human social network. How do humans interact, form friendships, and spread information? And how are we all affected by an ever changing network structure? Answering these questions will enrich our understanding of ourselves, our organizations, and our societies. Yet, mapping the dynamics of social networks has traditionally been an arduous undertaking. Today, however, it is possible to use the unprecedented amounts of information collected by mobile phones to gain detailed insight into the dynamics of social systems. This dissertation presents an unparalleled data collection campaign, collecting highly detailed traces for approximately 1000 people over the course of multiple years. The availability of such dynamic maps allows us to probe the underlying social network and understand how individuals interact and form lasting friendships. More importantly, these highly detailed dynamic maps provide us new perspectives at traditional problems and allow us to quantify and predict human life.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Sekara, Vedran"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-367551"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamics of high resolution networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dtp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/115674646/phd367_Sekara_V.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-367551","ids":["dtu-d2c065dc-22dc-4f3c-aa54-504038b669fe"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-239A9E085AA9ADE38B756778203B6D46"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/115674646/phd367_Sekara_V.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vedran","key":"sekarapau","last":"Sekara","locid":"2a6bd001-485b-4d3e-8210-d3ce9420c177","name":"Sekara, Vedran","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09093192"],"pages":"189","place":"Kgs. Lyngby","publisher":"Danmarks Tekniske Universitet (DTU)","series":"DTU Compute PHD","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d2c065dc-22dc-4f3c-aa54-504038b669fe"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Dynamics of High-Resolution Networks","type":"Thesis PhD","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-367551","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Understanding how people interact and socialize is important in many contexts from disease control to urban planning. Datasets that capture this specific aspect of human life have increased in size and availability over the last few years. We have yet to understand, however, to what extent such electronic datasets may serve as a valid proxy for real life social interactions. For an observational dataset, gathered using mobile phones, we analyze the problem of identifying transient and non-important links, as well as how to highlight important social interactions. Applying the Bluetooth signal strength parameter to distinguish between observations, we demonstrate that weak links, compared to strong links, have a lower probability of being observed at later times, while such links—on average—also have lower link-weights and probability of sharing an online friendship. Further, the role of link-strength is investigated in relation to social network properties.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sekara, Vedran","Lehmann, Sune"],"cuid":["S02-086.05-035200"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cell phones","Eagles","Graphs","Signal processing","Social networks","Telecommunications"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Cognitive Systems"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the strength of friendship ties in proximity sensor data","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/98238712/journal.pone.0100915.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.05-035200","identifier":[{"id":"84904336359","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4085074","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000338637300018","type":"wos"},{"id":"24999984","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-71e3ee75-7355-4113-a337-b8bfe594d8b6","ku-03c115b3-dd21-466b-b24a-39a164886911"],"keyword":["Cell phones","Eagles","Graphs","Signal filtering","Signal processing","Signaling networks","Social networks","Telecommunications"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3D17501834669BE3E96F27DB3AAD8418"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/98238712/journal.pone.0100915.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.plosone.org/article/info%3Adoi%2F10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0100915","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0100915","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Biocomplexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vedran","key":"sekarapau","last":"Sekara","locid":"2a6bd001-485b-4d3e-8210-d3ce9420c177","name":"Sekara, Vedran","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sune Lehmann","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"9049a0bd-7e6f-4f06-80f6-88ac447289e7","name":"Lehmann, Sune","name_org":"Jørgensen, Sune Lehmann","orcid":"0000-0001-6099-2345","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24999984"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0100915","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"7","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e100915","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84904336359"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-71e3ee75-7355-4113-a337-b8bfe594d8b6","ku-03c115b3-dd21-466b-b24a-39a164886911"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Strength of Friendship Ties in Proximity Sensor Data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.05-035200","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes the deployment of a large-scale study designed to measure human interactions across a variety of communication channels, with high temporal resolution and spanning multiple years-the Copenhagen Networks Study. Specifically, we collect data on face-to-face interactions, telecommunication, social networks, location, and background information (personality, demographics, health, politics) for a densely connected population of 1 000 individuals, using state-of-the-art smartphones as social sensors. Here we provide an overview of the related work and describe the motivation and research agenda driving the study. Additionally, the paper details the data-types measured, and the technical infrastructure in terms of both backend and phone software, as well as an outline of the deployment procedures. We document the participant privacy procedures and their underlying principles. The paper is concluded with early results from data analysis, illustrating the importance of multi-channel high-resolution approach to data collection.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Stopczynski, Arkadiusz","Sekara, Vedran","Sapiezynski, Piotr","Cuttone, Andrea","Madsen, Mette My","Larsen, Jakob Eg","Lehmann, Sune"],"cuid":["S02-081.98-036259"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Community","Dynamic networks","Multidisciplinary","Patterns","Personality traits","Predictability","Privacy","Reliability","Smartphones","Validity"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measuring large scale social networks with high resolution","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","ty